{
  "verdict": "request-changes",
  "head_sha": "e1f2532ea865da26887a7f3d0a1e92f682ff8d7d",
  "blocking_findings": [
    {
      "file": "src/IntentSystem.Cli/Commands/CrossRuntimeReviewRequestSupport.cs",
      "line": 65,
      "scenario": "TryValidateOutDir refuses any existing isolation directory because Path.Exists(path) is true even when the directory is empty. A second request using an out-dir containing only its own rendered files and empty copilot-home/copilot-xdg or opencode isolation directories therefore returns out-dir-not-empty, violating the required acceptance of empty existing directories and same-runtime re-rendering."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/IntentSystem.Cli.Tests/G842NoLaunchSourceGuardTests.cs",
      "line": 100,
      "scenario": "The source guard explicitly exempts DllImport, LibraryImport, and NativeLibrary in the new CrossRuntimeReviewFileMode.cs, which contains four new DllImport references beginning at line 132. AC10 requires unlisted launch tokens to fail and forbids allow-listing or otherwise exempting a CrossRuntime surface file, so the guard passes a prohibited new interop surface instead of failing closed."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/IntentSystem.Cli/Commands/CrossRuntimeReviewFileMode.cs",
      "line": 25,
      "scenario": "The non-macOS lstat parser reads st_mode at byte offset 12. On the supported linux-x64 target, struct stat stores st_mode at offset 24, so ordinary files are generally classified as non-regular. Consequently record --runtime opencode on Linux refuses a valid regular opencode-exit.txt containing exactly 0\\n as exit-status-missing; existing rendered files can also be rejected as non-regular."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/IntentSystem.Cli/Commands/CrossRuntimeReviewRuntimes.cs",
      "line": 122,
      "scenario": "The rendered Copilot read_only_enforcement omits the required credential dependency: with the isolated home Copilot runs gh auth token itself, and a signed-in real gh must be first on PATH. An operator relying on the request result is therefore not warned about the measured authentication requirement and can receive an immediate authentication failure, contrary to the explicit enforcement-text contract."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Command execution was unavailable in this runtime. I verified the requested SHA by reading .git/HEAD and reviewed the named target paths, but could not run git or tests or enumerate the commits absent from the base branch."
  ]
}
